The full licence text is in LICENSE, in this directory, reproduced
unchanged from the 7-Zip source distribution (DOC/License.txt). It is kept
here because the library in this directory is a binary distribution of
LGPL-covered code.

The unRAR licence restriction means the RAR decoding code may not be used
to develop a RAR (WinRAR) compatible archiver. This library only decodes
RAR archives; creating them is left to RARLAB's own rar program, which the
user installs.

The library is linked statically. Its complete source, including the C
interface, is published at the release and branch recorded in SOURCE, and
MacRAR's own source is public, so the application can be rebuilt and
relinked against a modified build of this library, as the LGPL asks.

This build comes from a fork that adds the C interface and its build and
release scripts in a directory of its own and leaves 7-Zip's sources
unmodified. The fork adds no copyright line of its own to 7-Zip's files.

MacRAR is not affiliated with the 7-Zip project. Its name appears here only
to identify the software this library was built from, not to endorse or
promote MacRAR.
